course: dictionary
lesson: 13462
title: Adverbs that show how: humorously
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An adverb tells us how, when or where something happens. Humorously is an adverb. It tells us how someone does something, and it means in a funny way that makes people smile or laugh. «The poem is written humorously.» This tells us the poem is funny in the way it is written.
explain: Spot an adverb by its -ly ending, and by asking how something is done. The family words are humor (noun), humorous (adjective) and humorously (adverb). «The clown bowed humorously» tells us how the clown bowed: with a funny little wobble, not a serious one.
explain: Use context to check your meaning. Swap in «in a funny way» and see if the sentence still makes sense. «She told the story humorously, and the whole class giggled.» If the class giggles, the story was told in a funny way, so humorously fits.
fact: Humorously is an adverb, so it describes how an action is done.
fact: «Humorously» means in a funny way that makes people smile or laugh.
fact: The adjective is humorous, as in «a humorous poem».
fact: Phrases to remember: speak humorously, and humorously written.
fact: Many adverbs are made by adding -ly to an adjective, so check the root word first.
exercise: «The clown bowed humorously and the crowd laughed.» What does humorously mean here? | In a very quiet way | In a sad and slow way | *In a funny way that makes people smile | Very quickly and angrily
exercise: «The poem is written humorously.» Which word tells us how the poem is written? | written | is | poem | *humorously
exercise: Ayesha says humorous and humorously are the same kind of word. Which word is an adverb? | *humorously | humor | funny | poem
test: Grandma told the joke humorously, and everyone laughed. What does humorously tell us about how Grandma told the joke? | In a shy and quiet way | In a serious and worried way | *In a funny way that made everyone laugh | In a loud and angry way
test: Which sentence shows someone acting in a funny way? | The sky was humorously grey. | She counted humorously to ten. | The river flowed humorously past the bridge. | *The uncle in the play spoke humorously, and the audience giggled.
exam: Which word means in a funny way that makes people smile? | Sadly | Slowly | *Humorously | Humbly
